### 1.4 Behaviour changes a reviewer must know about
1. `ed25519IsStrictPoint` now requires torsion-free points (CP-04). Measured cost: Ed25519 verify 2.76 ms -> 5.53 ms per verification (strict-point check 0.12 ms -> 1.5 ms). The server e2e was not measurably slower (32.4 s vs 33.6 s). If verification becomes a bottleneck, cache torsion-freeness per public key and replace the per-signature R check with a cofactorless comparison of the encoded R.
2. `analyzeBallotLog` drops a spoil that shares ElGamal `a` values with an envelope-valid cast under a different code, with ALARM `E_SPOILED_CODE_CAST` ("re-wrapped") (CP-01/TR-01). Same-code behaviour unchanged.
3. `verifyElection`: a second, different tally record is `E_RESULT` F (P3); a spoil with a bad attached reveal still spoils its code (P4); `chk.tally.decrypt` is `pass` only after decryption ran (P7); `tally.decrypters` must equal the recomputed set and `buildTally` emits it (P11). The canary vector `expected-report.json` therefore has `chk.tally.decrypt: not_run`; vectors were regenerated (`node packages/protocol/test/vecgen/write.ts`).
4. Crypto: scrypt `logN` cap lowered 22 -> 20 on open (bundles sealed at 21/22 can no longer be opened; none exist in the repo) with optional `maxLogN`; `canonicalize` throws on non-plain objects, non-NFC strings, lone-surrogate keys.
5. Server: `GET log/entries` pages may hold fewer than `limit` rows (`maxPageBytes`, default 4 MiB): clients must follow `next_from`; link-election responses are `private, no-store`; new non-log endpoints `POST|GET /api/v1/elections/:id/spoil-shares`; electiondb migration 4 `spoil_share`.
6. Trustee: tally release now requires the trustee to have imported `election-open` (STANDBY) (the other session's gate); two processes on one bundle fail fast (`BUNDLE_LOCKED`/`BUNDLE_CHANGED`; a hard kill leaves `<bundle>.lock` which the operator deletes by hand); fork refusal `LOG_FORK` at release.
7. CLI: `board verify` without `--log-key` on a standalone board bundle is PARTIAL (exit 3); new `--witness-policy`, `--manifest-hash` on `ballot encrypt|audit`; new `qv election spoil-collect`.
8. Web: post-send failures are PENDING_UNCONFIRMED and retry the same sealed bytes; receipt heads are checked against the pinned head; a tally counts only if signed by a manifest coordinator key under ctx; auto-lock reaches an open ballot session.
9. CI: new lockfile lint and high/critical audit gates (ubuntu node 22 only).

